WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.960 --> 00:00:02.419
- This is it.

00:00:02.419 --> 00:00:04.213
This is the beans on the toast.

00:00:04.910 --> 00:00:08.342
(funky guitar music)

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:11.470
- I've had beans, and I've had toast.

00:00:11.470 --> 00:00:13.681
I've never had beans on toast.

00:00:13.681 --> 00:00:15.808
- I've never heard of beans on toast.

00:00:15.808 --> 00:00:17.840
I've usually heard that beans

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:20.646
are best served with barbecue.

00:00:21.022 --> 00:00:23.315
- I'm a big fan of all the components, so

00:00:23.315 --> 00:00:25.485
I expect it's going to be delicious.

00:00:25.485 --> 00:00:28.352
- The beans just look like, ugh.

00:00:28.352 --> 00:00:30.322
Like Spaghetti-Os gone wrong.

00:00:30.322 --> 00:00:32.366
- You know, it smells almost like nothing.

00:00:32.366 --> 00:00:35.238
- Golly, it looks like
a vegetarian sloppy joe.

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.874
- It smells so nasty.

00:00:39.874 --> 00:00:41.667
- You know, this isn't bad.

00:00:41.667 --> 00:00:45.337
- The bread is the exact same
consistency as the beans.

00:00:45.337 --> 00:00:47.938
- Yeah, it tastes like the 4th of July.

00:00:48.738 --> 00:00:50.625
Which for a British
food is pretty awkward.

00:00:50.625 --> 00:00:51.928
- I don't know what I think.

00:00:51.928 --> 00:00:53.262
- I'm sorry; I don't like it.

00:00:53.262 --> 00:00:56.056
- It just tastes like totally edible,

00:00:56.056 --> 00:00:58.435
flavorless beans on toast.

00:00:58.435 --> 00:01:00.561
- I've eaten a lot of other weird things

00:01:00.561 --> 00:01:02.730
and this is definitely not
the weirdest thing I've eaten.

00:01:02.730 --> 00:01:04.523
I don't know why people are confused.

00:01:04.523 --> 00:01:05.733
- Right, I mean, that's what I see.

00:01:05.733 --> 00:01:07.944
I see a lot of lonely British men

00:01:07.944 --> 00:01:11.322
going home to their flats and
preparing this for dinner,

00:01:11.322 --> 00:01:12.698
wishing they had a wife.

00:01:12.698 --> 00:01:15.243
- I think beans on toast
will catch on in America

00:01:15.243 --> 00:01:17.203
because Americans love beans.

00:01:17.203 --> 00:01:19.288
Everyone loves beans, and I don't get it.

00:01:19.288 --> 00:01:22.333
- I mean, hey, we all have
our things that we eat

00:01:22.333 --> 00:01:24.428
that are different, and you know what,

00:01:24.428 --> 00:01:27.254
if it works for you, then why the hell not

00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:29.131
put beans on toast.

00:01:29.131 --> 00:01:31.216
- All right, okay, if I were
going to make beans on toast

00:01:31.216 --> 00:01:35.339
it would be wholegrain bread, guacamole,

00:01:35.339 --> 00:01:37.889
black beans, (mumbles).

00:01:37.889 --> 00:01:40.268
And that's basically already at Chipotle.

